# Remove SDL from the desktop Clients

Status: authorized; implementation on `client-no-sdl`, based on dependency-refresh
root `e7f10d73c14c` and Client `7813e7b408d51ce890a926d6315530b0f678191c`.
The existing 1.2.14 dependency candidates are the comparison checkpoint.
The operator selected version 1.3.00 for this change. Candidates use
`1.3.00-client-no-sdl` in package filenames and the visible application version;
subsequent builds increment the shared version normally.

## Contract

Keep Qt session windows and controls, Linux EGL/VA-API and PipeWire, and Mac
Metal/VideoToolbox. Preserve exact codec/color qualification, audio/video
synchronization, native input/Wacom ownership, microphone permissions, clipboard,
network recovery and installed identities. Host and wire protocols do not change.
Mac Client remains Apple Silicon/macOS 15+, built with SDK 27+. Do not substitute
Qt Multimedia decoding, an SDL compatibility layer or new user preferences.

## Implementation

1. Remove the superseded SDL session/window/rendering path. Reduce common decoder,
   overlay and display interfaces to what the Qt clients use. Retain upstream
   attribution and independently useful regression tests.
2. Replace live SDL utility calls with Qt/standard C++: one monotonic clock,
   bounded queues, synchronized stop predicates, ordinary threads/mutexes,
   product logging and platform-independent keyboard events.
3. Keep Linux playback/capture on direct PipeWire. Replace the remaining capture
   fallback without changing microphone protocol negotiation.
4. Add native Core Audio playback and microphone capture on Mac. Preserve the
   accepted resampling/controller policy, audio-device latency accounting,
   bounded callback buffers, OS-selected devices and device-change recovery.
   Audio callbacks must not allocate, block on the GUI, or log.
5. Remove SDL/SDL_ttf from bootstrap, cache fingerprints, linking, packages and
   tests. Require clean candidate binaries/package payloads with no SDL linkage.
   Keep unrelated Host dependencies and unfinished Apple-native/AVP work separate.

## Verification

Use GitHub-hosted Linux and Mac builds. Exercise Qt lifecycle, input/key release,
Wacom detach/recovery, overlays, exact 8/10-bit color, 4K/5K, network recovery,
audio clock/resampling/starvation, microphone and cleanup fixtures. Preserve
hardware-dependent skips honestly. Check package contents, dependency closure,
minimum OS, signing and branch-qualified version/provenance. No merge or release.

Installed acceptance still requires both Host platforms, long A/V listening
soaks, output/input device changes, mute/permissions, Wacom, fullscreen/Spaces and
reconnect tests on supported Client OS versions. Do not interrupt active users
or install on an end-user machine without authorization.
